<!-- 1. INTRODUCTION -->
<div class="section-break">
<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
The Crane &amp; JCB ERP System is a comprehensive, cloud-based business management platform
designed specifically for crane rental and JCB operations companies. It handles every aspect
of the business &mdash; from vehicle and driver management to trip logging, billing, invoicing,
diesel tracking, maintenance, EMI management, salary advances, attendance, and financial reporting.
</p>
<p>
The system replaces manual ledgers, Excel spreadsheets, and disconnected tools with a single,
unified platform that works across desktop computers, tablets, and mobile phones. All data is
stored securely in the cloud and updates in real-time across all devices.
</p>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Key Benefits at a Glance</h4>
<ul>
<li><b>Real-time visibility</b> &mdash; Know exactly which vehicles are working, available, or under maintenance at any moment</li>
<li><b>Automated billing</b> &mdash; Generate cash bills and GST-compliant invoices directly from trip entries with zero double-entry</li>
<li><b>Versioned rate master</b> &mdash; Rate changes are tracked with effective dates, so old trips retain the rates that were active at the time</li>
<li><b>Financial reporting</b> &mdash; Profit &amp; loss, monthly summaries, diesel costs, and salary statements at your fingertips</li>
<li><b>Bilingual</b> &mdash; Full English and Telugu language support with a single click</li>
<li><b>Secure &amp; role-based</b> &mdash; Admin, Manager, and Operator roles with appropriate access controls</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<!-- 2. DASHBOARD -->
<div class="section-break">
<h2>2. System Dashboard</h2>
<p>
The Dashboard is the first screen users see after logging in. It provides a real-time snapshot
of the entire business with live-updating KPI cards and summary tables.
</p>

<h3>Vehicle Status Overview</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Metric</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Total Vehicles</td><td>Count of all vehicles in the system</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active Vehicles</td><td>Vehicles currently marked as active</td></tr>
<tr><td>Available</td><td>Vehicles ready for assignment (not currently on a trip)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Working</td><td>Vehicles currently on an active trip/job</td></tr>
<tr><td>Under Maintenance</td><td>Vehicles undergoing repairs or servicing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inactive</td><td>Vehicles not in active fleet rotation</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Today's Operations Summary</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Metric</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Trips</td><td>Number of trips logged for the current date</td></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Revenue</td><td>Total rental + batha amount from today's trips</td></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Diesel Cost</td><td>Total diesel expenses logged today</td></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Maintenance</td><td>Maintenance costs incurred today</td></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Batha</td><td>Total operator batha from today's trips</td></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Cash Collection</td><td>Cash payments collected today</td></tr>
<tr><td>Today's Online Collection</td><td>Online/bank transfer payments collected today</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pending Customer Amount</td><td>Unpaid amounts from today's trips</td></tr>
<tr><td>EMI Due / Overdue</td><td>Vehicle loan EMI alerts</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Monthly Summary</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Metric</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly Revenue</td><td>Total revenue for the current month</td></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly Expenses</td><td>Diesel + Batha + Maintenance costs for the month</td></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly Profit/Loss</td><td>Revenue minus expenses, with profit or loss indicator</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Today's Vehicle Summary Table</h3>
<p>
A live table showing each vehicle that has a trip today, with customizable columns.
Users can choose which fields to display (date, vehicle, driver, customer, hours, rental, batha,
total, payment status, etc.) and the selection is remembered automatically.
</p>

<div class="highlight-box">
<h4>EMI Alerts</h4>
<p>
The dashboard automatically displays alerts for upcoming and overdue vehicle EMI payments,
ensuring you never miss a loan installment.
</p>
</div>
</div>

<!-- 3. MASTER DATA -->
<div class="section-break">
<h2>3. Master Data Management</h2>
<p>
Master data forms the foundation of the system. These are the core records that all daily
operations and billing reference.
</p>

<h3>3.1 Crane/Vehicle Master</h3>
<p>
A complete registry of all cranes and JCBs in the fleet. Each vehicle record captures:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Serial Number</td><td>Internal serial number for the vehicle</td></tr>
<tr><td>Registration Number</td><td>Official RTO registration number</td></tr>
<tr><td>Model</td><td>Vehicle model/make (e.g., Tata, Bharat Benz)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Type</td><td>Crane or JCB</td></tr>
<tr><td>Capacity / Tons</td><td>Crane capacity in tons (e.g., 15 Tons) or JCB designation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hourly Rate</td><td>Default first-hour rate (used as fallback if Rate Master is not configured)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily Rate</td><td>Default full-day rate</td></tr>
<tr><td>Status</td><td>Available, Working, Maintenance, or Inactive</td></tr>
<tr><td>EMI Status</td><td>Whether this vehicle has an active EMI (loan installment)</td></tr>
<tr><td>EMI Amount &amp; Due Date</td><td>Monthly EMI amount and next due date</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active</td><td>Whether the vehicle is part of the active fleet</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.2 Employee Master</h3>
<p>
A registry of all employees &mdash; drivers, operators, helpers, and other staff. Each record includes:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Name</td><td>Full name of the employee</td></tr>
<tr><td>Role</td><td>Driver, Operator, Helper, or Other</td></tr>
<tr><td>Phone</td><td>Contact number</td></tr>
<tr><td>Salary</td><td>Monthly salary amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>License Number</td><td>Driving license number</td></tr>
<tr><td>License Expiry</td><td>License renewal date (for compliance tracking)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advance Salary</td><td>Outstanding salary advance amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active</td><td>Whether the employee is currently employed</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Employee Smart Features</h4>
<ul>
<li><b>License expiry alerts</b> &mdash; Expired licenses are flagged in red; licenses expiring within 30 days show a warning indicator</li>
<li><b>Role-based filtering</b> &mdash; Filter the employee list by role (Driver, Operator, Helper, Other) or status (Active, Inactive)</li>
<li><b>Safe deletion</b> &mdash; If an employee has attendance or trip records, the system deactivates them instead of deleting, preserving all historical data</li>
<li><b>Excel export</b> &mdash; Export the full employee master with company branding and applied filters</li>
<li><b>License fields conditional</b> &mdash; License number and expiry fields appear only for Driver and Operator roles</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h3>3.3 Rate Master (Versioned)</h3>
<p>
The Rate Master is one of the most powerful features of the system. It allows you to define
rental rates for different vehicle categories (e.g., 15 Ton Crane, JCB) with full version control:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Vehicle Category</td><td>Category name (e.g., "15 Ton", "JCB")</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vehicle Type</td><td>Crane or JCB</td></tr>
<tr><td>Capacity / Tons</td><td>Capacity in tons for cranes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rate Type</td><td>Hourly, Daily, Both, Couple Hours, or Monthly</td></tr>
<tr><td>1st Hour Rate</td><td>Charge for the first hour</td></tr>
<tr><td>2nd Hour Rate</td><td>Charge for the second hour</td></tr>
<tr><td>3rd, 4th, 5th Hour Rates</td><td>Progressive hourly rates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Couple Hours Rate</td><td>Special rate for 2-hour jobs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily Rate</td><td>Full-day rental rate</td></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly Rate</td><td>Monthly contract rate</td></tr>
<tr><td>Batha</td><td>Standard operator batha amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Effective From / To</td><td>Date range when this rate version is active</td></tr>
<tr><td>Status</td><td>Active, Inactive, or Closed</td></tr>
<tr><td>Version Number</td><td>Auto-incremented version for audit trail</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>How Versioned Rates Work</h4>
<p>
When a trip is logged, the system automatically looks up the correct Rate Master entry based
on the vehicle type, capacity, and trip date. The rates are "snapshotted" (saved permanently)
on the trip record. This means if you change rates tomorrow, all past trips retain the rates
that were active when the trip was created &mdash; ensuring historical accuracy for billing and audits.
</p>
</div>

<h3>3.4 Customer Master</h3>
<p>
A complete database of all customers with billing and shipping details:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Name</td><td>Customer or company name</td></tr>
<tr><td>Address</td><td>Billing address</td></tr>
<tr><td>Phone &amp; Email</td><td>Contact information</td></tr>
<tr><td>GSTIN</td><td>GST identification number (for GST invoices)</td></tr>
<tr><td>State &amp; State Code</td><td>State and GST state code (for intra-state vs inter-state GST)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment Terms</td><td>Default payment terms (e.g., 30 days)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shipping Address</td><td>Delivery/ship-to address (if different from billing)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active</td><td>Whether the customer is currently active</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3.5 Monthly Contracts</h3>
<p>
For customers on monthly billing arrangements, the system supports monthly contracts with:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Company Name</td><td>Name of the contract company</td></tr>
<tr><td>Address</td><td>Company address</td></tr>
<tr><td>Billing Details</td><td>Specific billing instructions or terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Allocated Vehicle</td><td>Vehicle assigned to this contract</td></tr>
<tr><td>Start Date</td><td>Contract start date</td></tr>
<tr><td>End Date</td><td>Contract end date (optional for open-ended contracts)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Contract budget amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total Monthly Amount</td><td>Monthly billing amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Status</td><td>Active, Completed, Expired, or Cancelled</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Contract Management Features</h4>
<ul>
<li><b>Full CRUD</b> &mdash; Create, edit, and delete contracts with confirmation prompts</li>
<li><b>Vehicle assignment</b> &mdash; Link a specific vehicle from the fleet to each contract</li>
<li><b>Searchable list</b> &mdash; Search contracts by company name</li>
<li><b>Status tracking</b> &mdash; Visual status badges for Active, Completed, Expired, and Cancelled contracts</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<!-- 4. DAILY OPERATIONS -->
<div class="section-break">
<h2>4. Daily Operations</h2>

<h3>4.1 Trip Entries</h3>
<p>
The Trip Entry is the heart of the system. Every job &mdash; whether it's a crane rental or a JCB
assignment &mdash; is recorded as a trip. The system automatically calculates rental amounts based
on the Rate Master, vehicle type, and hours worked.
</p>

<h4>What a Trip Entry Captures</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Trip Number</td><td>Auto-generated unique trip ID (never null, never duplicated)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Trip Date</td><td>Date of the job</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Selected from active fleet (filtered by tons/capacity)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Driver / Operator</td><td>Assigned driver or operator</td></tr>
<tr><td>Customer</td><td>Customer for this trip (optional)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Place of Work</td><td>Job location</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rate Type</td><td>Hourly, Full Day, Couple Hours, or Monthly</td></tr>
<tr><td>In Time / Out Time</td><td>Start and end time of the job</td></tr>
<tr><td>Opening / Closing Hour Meter</td><td>Meter readings (auto-suggests last closing as opening)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total Hours</td><td>Auto-calculated from meter readings or time entries</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rental Amount</td><td>Auto-calculated from Rate Master or vehicle rates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Batha</td><td>Auto-filled from Rate Master (editable if needed)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total Amount</td><td>Rental + Batha (auto-calculated)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bill Status</td><td>Paid or Pending (toggle with one click)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment Mode</td><td>Cash, Online, Bank Transfer, or Other</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment Date</td><td>Date when payment was received</td></tr>
<tr><td>Remarks</td><td>Any additional notes</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Smart Rate Calculation</h4>
<p>
The system automatically determines the rental amount using this priority:
</p>
<ol>
<li><b>Rate Master</b> (highest priority) &mdash; looks up the active rate version matching the vehicle type, capacity, and trip date</li>
<li><b>Legacy Rate Table</b> &mdash; falls back to the older rates table if no Rate Master match is found</li>
<li><b>Vehicle Default Rates</b> &mdash; falls back to the vehicle's own hourly/daily rate</li>
</ol>
<p>
For hourly jobs, the system calculates: 1st hour at the 1st-hour rate, 2nd hour at the 2nd-hour
rate, and subsequent hours at the applicable progressive rate. For full-day jobs, the daily rate
is applied. For couple-hour jobs, the special couple-hours rate is used.
</p>
</div>

<h4>Trip Entry Features</h4>
<ul>
<li><b>Vehicle filtering by tons</b> &mdash; Select the crane capacity first, then only matching vehicles appear</li>
<li><b>Auto meter carry-forward</b> &mdash; The opening meter auto-fills with the last trip's closing meter</li>
<li><b>Live billing preview</b> &mdash; See the rental calculation breakdown before saving</li>
<li><b>Payment status toggle</b> &mdash; Mark trips as Paid/Pending right from the entry form</li>
<li><b>Customizable table columns</b> &mdash; Choose which fields to show and export</li>
<li><b>Excel export</b> &mdash; Export all trips with company branding and selected fields</li>
<li><b>Payment totals dashboard</b> &mdash; Total amount, paid, pending, and trip counts at a glance</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2 Diesel Entry</h3>
<p>
Track all diesel/fuel purchases for each vehicle with full payment tracking:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Date</td><td>Date of diesel purchase</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pump Name</td><td>Name of the fuel station</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Vehicle that received the fuel</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quantity (Liters)</td><td>Amount of diesel purchased</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rate per Liter</td><td>Price per liter</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total Amount</td><td>Auto-calculated (quantity x rate)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Paid Amount</td><td>Amount paid at the time of purchase</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pending Amount</td><td>Outstanding balance (auto-calculated)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment Status</td><td>Paid, Pending, or Partially Paid</td></tr>
<tr><td>Remarks</td><td>Additional notes</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>4.3 Attendance</h3>
<p>
Daily attendance tracking for all employees:
</p>
<ul>
<li>Mark employees as Present, Absent, or Holiday for any date</li>
<li>Bulk attendance entry for a selected date</li>
<li>View attendance history per employee</li>
<li>Integrates with salary calculations</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.4 Maintenance</h3>
<p>
Track all vehicle maintenance and repair expenses:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Date</td><td>Date of maintenance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vehicle</td><td>Vehicle that underwent maintenance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Type</td><td>Tyre, Repair, or Others</td></tr>
<tr><td>Amount</td><td>Cost of maintenance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Description</td><td>Details of the work performed</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>4.5 EMI Management</h3>
<p>
Track vehicle loan EMIs with status tracking:
</p>
<ul>
<li>Record EMI amount, due date, and payment status for each vehicle</li>
<li>Status: Upcoming, Due, Paid, or Overdue</li>
<li>Dashboard alerts for due and overdue EMIs</li>
<li>Payment mode tracking (Cash, Online, Bank Transfer)</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.6 Salary Advance Management</h3>
<p>
The system includes a dedicated Salary Advance module to track employee advances and recoveries:
</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Advance Date</td><td>Date the advance was given</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advance Reference</td><td>Reference number or identifier for the advance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advance Amount</td><td>Amount given as advance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reason</td><td>Purpose of the advance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment Mode</td><td>Cash, Bank Transfer, UPI, or Other</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reference Number</td><td>Transaction reference number</td></tr>
<tr><td>Status</td><td>Outstanding, Partially Recovered, or Fully Recovered</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>Recovery Tracking</h4>
<p>
When an employee's salary is processed, advance recoveries can be recorded against outstanding
advances. Each recovery tracks:
</p>
<ul>
<li>Recovery date and salary month</li>
<li>Recovery amount</li>
<li>Linked to the original advance record</li>
<li>Remarks for audit trail</li>
</ul>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Salary Statement Report</h4>
<p>
The Salary Statement report combines base salary, advances taken, recoveries made, and attendance
data to calculate the net payable amount for each employee per month. This gives a complete picture
of payroll obligations at any time.
</p>
</div>
</div>

<!-- 5. BILLING -->
<div class="section-break">
<h2>5. Billing &amp; Invoicing</h2>

<h3>5.1 Cash Bills</h3>
<p>
Cash Bills are simple, non-GST bills generated from completed trip entries. They are ideal for
walk-in customers or jobs that don't require a GST invoice.
</p>

<h4>How It Works</h4>
<ol>
<li>Select a customer (or leave blank for walk-in customers)</li>
<li>The system shows all pending (un-invoiced) trips for that customer</li>
<li>Select one or more trips to include in the cash bill</li>
<li>Preview the bill with all details (vehicle type, trip date, hours, rental, batha, total)</li>
<li>Generate and print the cash bill</li>
</ol>

<h4>Cash Bill Contents</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Section</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Company Header</td><td>Company name, address, phone, GSTIN</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bill Number</td><td>Auto-generated sequential number</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bill Date</td><td>Date of bill generation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Customer Details</td><td>Name and address</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vehicle Info</td><td>Vehicle number, type (e.g., "15 Tons" for cranes, "JCB" for JCBs)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Trip Details</td><td>Date, place of work, hours, driver name</td></tr>
<tr><td>Amounts</td><td>Rental amount, batha, total amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Amount in Words</td><td>Total amount converted to words</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Vehicle Type Display</h4>
<p>
The system intelligently displays vehicle types:
</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Cranes</b> &mdash; shown as "15 Tons" (or whatever the capacity is)</li>
<li><b>JCBs</b> &mdash; shown as "JCB"</li>
</ul>
<p>This display is consistent across cash bills, customer invoices, and all reports.</p>
</div>

<h3>5.2 Customer Invoices (GST)</h3>
<p>
Customer Invoices are full, GST-compliant tax invoices designed for B2B billing. They support
both intra-state (CGST + SGST) and inter-state (IGST) GST calculations.
</p>

<h4>How It Works</h4>
<ol>
<li>Select a customer from the customer master</li>
<li>The system displays all pending trips for that customer (trips not yet linked to an invoice)</li>
<li>Select one or more trips to include in the invoice</li>
<li>The system auto-generates line items from the selected trips, including:
  <ul>
    <li>Description with vehicle type, trip date, vehicle number, place, and hours</li>
    <li>HSN/SAC code (configurable in settings)</li>
    <li>Quantity, rate, and amount per trip</li>
    <li>Operator batha as a separate line item (consolidated)</li>
  </ul>
</li>
<li>Choose GST type: Intra-State (CGST + SGST) or Inter-State (IGST)</li>
<li>Adjust GST percentages if needed (defaults from settings)</li>
<li>Add consignee (ship-to) details if different from bill-to</li>
<li>Add invoice metadata: destination, terms of payment, buyer's order no, reference no, dispatch doc no, delivery note date</li>
<li>Preview the invoice in a print-ready format</li>
<li>Generate the invoice &mdash; the system auto-generates an invoice number and marks all selected trips as "Invoiced"</li>
</ol>

<h4>Invoice Contents</h4>
<table>
<tr><th>Section</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Company Header</td><td>Company name, address, phone, email, GSTIN</td></tr>
<tr><td>Invoice Number</td><td>Auto-generated with configurable prefix (e.g., PCS-2026-001)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Invoice Date</td><td>Date of invoice generation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Financial Year</td><td>Auto-calculated (e.g., 2026-27)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bill To (Customer)</td><td>Name, address, GSTIN, state, state code</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ship To (Consignee)</td><td>Same as bill-to or separate consignee details</td></tr>
<tr><td>Line Items</td><td>One row per trip with description, HSN/SAC, qty, rate, amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Operator Batha</td><td>Consolidated batha as a separate line item</td></tr>
<tr><td>Taxable Amount</td><td>Sum of rental amounts + batha</td></tr>
<tr><td>CGST &amp; SGST</td><td>For intra-state (each 9% by default, configurable)</td></tr>
<tr><td>IGST</td><td>For inter-state (18% by default, configurable)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Grand Total</td><td>Taxable amount + total GST</td></tr>
<tr><td>Amount in Words</td><td>Grand total converted to words</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bank Details</td><td>Bank name, account name, account number, branch, IFSC</td></tr>
<tr><td>Declaration</td><td>Configurable declaration text</td></tr>
<tr><td>Authorized Signatory</td><td>Name and signature/stamp</td></tr>
<tr><td>Terms of Payment</td><td>Payment terms (e.g., 30 days)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Additional Fields</td><td>Destination, delivery note, buyer's order no, reference no, dispatch doc no</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>Invoice Management</h4>
<ul>
<li><b>View</b> &mdash; Open any invoice in a print-ready preview</li>
<li><b>Print</b> &mdash; Print directly to any connected printer</li>
<li><b>Excel Export</b> &mdash; Export invoice details to Excel with company branding</li>
<li><b>Record Payment</b> &mdash; Record partial or full payments against an invoice</li>
<li><b>Payment History</b> &mdash; View all payments made against an invoice</li>
<li><b>Cancel Invoice</b> &mdash; Cancel an invoice (keeps it for audit, marks trips as billable again)</li>
<li><b>Delete Invoice</b> &mdash; Permanently delete (admin only), unlinks trips for re-billing</li>
<li><b>Status Tracking</b> &mdash; Draft, Generated, Paid, Partially Paid, Cancelled</li>
</ul>

<div class="highlight-box">
<h4>Invoice-Trip Linkage</h4>
<p>
When an invoice is generated, the system <b>updates the existing trip records</b> to link them
to the invoice. It does NOT create new trips or overwrite trip data. This ensures data integrity:
the original trip entry (with its auto-generated trip number, meter readings, and rate snapshot)
remains unchanged. The invoice simply references the trips by their IDs.
</p>
</div>
</div>

<!-- 6. REPORTS -->
<div class="section-break">
<h2>6. Reports &amp; Analytics</h2>
<p>
The system provides a comprehensive suite of reports, all with date-range filtering and
Excel export with company branding:
</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Report</th><th>What It Shows</th></tr>
<tr><td>Trip Report</td><td>All trips within a date range with vehicle, driver, customer, hours, rental, batha, total, and payment status</td></tr>
<tr><td>Diesel Report</td><td>All diesel entries with pump name, vehicle, quantity, rate, total, paid, pending, and payment status</td></tr>
<tr><td>Attendance Report</td><td>Employee attendance records with present/absent/holiday status</td></tr>
<tr><td>Maintenance Report</td><td>All maintenance records with vehicle, type, amount, and description</td></tr>
<tr><td>EMI Report</td><td>Vehicle EMI records with status, due dates, and payment tracking</td></tr>
<tr><td>Salary Statement</td><td>Employee salary details including advances, recoveries, and net payable</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily Vehicle Report</td><td>Day-by-day breakdown per vehicle showing trips, diesel, and maintenance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Monthly Report</td><td>Month-by-month summary of revenue, diesel, maintenance, batha, and profit</td></tr>
<tr><td>Profit &amp; Loss</td><td>Revenue vs. expenses (diesel + batha + maintenance) for any date range, showing net profit or loss</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cash Bill Report</td><td>All cash bills generated within a date range</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="feature-box">
<h4>Excel Export Features</h4>
<p>
All reports can be exported to Excel/CSV format with:
</p>
<ul>
<li>Company name, address, and contact details as header</li>
<li>Date range and generation date</li>
<li>Properly formatted columns with currency formatting</li>
<li>Summary/totals row where applicable</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

